      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To determine which number between 1 and 15 has the greatest number of divisors, we can directly calculate the number of divisors for each number. We'll use Python to ensure the accuracy of our calculations.\n\nHere's a step-by-step approach:\n\n1. Define a function to calculate the number of divisors of a given number.\n2. Iterate over each number from 1 to 15, calculate its number of divisors, and keep track of the number with the maximum number of divisors.\n\nLet's write the code to perform these steps:\n```python\ndef count_divisors(n):\n    count = 0\n    for i in range(1, n + 1):\n        if n % i == 0:\n            count += 1\n    return count\n\nmax_divisors = 0\nnumber_with_max_divisors = 0\n\n# Iterate over each number from 1 to 15\nfor i in range(1, 16):\n    divisors_count = count_divisors(i)\n    if divisors_count > max_divisors:\n        max_divisors = divisors_count\n        number_with_max_divisors = i\n\nprint((number_with_max_divisors, max_divisors))\n```\n```output\n(12, 6)\n```\nThe number between 1 and 15 that has the greatest number of divisors is \\(\\boxed{12}\\). It has exactly 6 divisors, which is more than any other number in that range.",
